From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>
Date: Wed, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-mhdp8546: Handle no-firmware passthrough
 mode for PSDK Analytics

On J784S4 EVM with PSDK Analytics SYSFW (Fancy Rat, 11.02.x), the
MHDP DP bridge MMIO SRAM (first 128 KB at 0xa000000) is firewalled for
the A72 host.  Any attempt by Linux to write the Cadence MHDP8546
firmware image into that SRAM via memcpy_toio() causes the SoC firewall
to raise an Asynchronous SError Interrupt, crashing the kernel.

With CONFIG_DRM_CDNS_MHDP8546=y the firmware write happens at
device_initcall time.  Even without the write (firmware absent,
error -ENOENT), cdns_mhdp_fw_cb() returns without setting
mhdp->plugged, so the DRM connector remains permanently "disconnected".
The downstream TIDSS bridge cannot find any encoder/connector chain and
Weston fails to start with "DRM: head 'DP-1' found, connector N is
disconnected."

However, U-Boot initializes the MHDP firmware (writing it to SRAM
before SYSFW locks the firewall) and trains the DP link during its
display initialisation.  That firmware remains running across the Linux
boot.  AUX channel and mailbox operations therefore work from Linux
even though the SRAM is subsequently firewalled.

Fix by entering a "no-firmware passthrough" mode when the firmware file
is absent:

  cdns_mhdp_fw_cb(): when fw is NULL, set mhdp->plugged = true under
  the start_lock spinlock and wake fw_load_wq.  hw_state intentionally
  remains MHDP_HW_STOPPED so that cdns_mhdp_attach() does NOT enable
  the HPD SW-event interrupt.  Enabling HPD would trigger
  cdns_mhdp_update_link_status() -> cdns_mhdp_link_up() before EDID is
  read, leaving stale mailbox responses that cause DPTX_GET_EDID to
  fail with -EINVAL.

  cdns_mhdp_atomic_enable() calls cdns_mhdp_link_up() when
  mhdp->plugged && !mhdp->link_up, independently of hw_state, so link
  training proceeds correctly once the compositor sets a mode.  If no
  firmware is running at all, the mailbox operations in
  cdns_mhdp_link_up() will time out and return an error, which the
  existing goto-out handling catches gracefully.

With these changes:
  - DRM connector DP-1 reports "connected".
  - EDID is read via AUX (U-Boot firmware handles the mailbox request),
    exposing the monitor's native resolution (e.g. 2560x1440).
  - cdns_mhdp_link_up() trains the DP link using the existing firmware
    when the compositor first sets a mode (not on HPD interrupt).
  - TIDSS DMA scanout produces physical display output on DP0.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TI J784S4 EVM PSDK Analytics SYSFW display enablement]

Signed-off-by: Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-mhdp8546-core.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-mhdp8546-core.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-mhdp8546-core.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-mhdp8546-core.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-mhdp8546-core.c
@@ -791,6 +791,21 @@

 	if (!fw || !fw->data) {
 		dev_err(mhdp->dev, "%s: No firmware.\n", __func__);
+		/* No firmware image on the filesystem, but U-Boot may have
+		 * loaded MHDP firmware into SRAM before the PSDK Analytics
+		 * SYSFW firewall locked the MHDP SRAM for the A72 host.
+		 * Set plugged=true so the DRM connector reports "connected"
+		 * and EDID can be read via AUX.  Leave hw_state as
+		 * MHDP_HW_STOPPED intentionally: this prevents attach() from
+		 * enabling the HPD interrupt, which would trigger early link
+		 * training and corrupt the EDID mailbox exchange.
+		 * cdns_mhdp_atomic_enable() triggers link training via the
+		 * plugged && !link_up path when the compositor sets a mode.
+		 */
+		spin_lock(&mhdp->start_lock);
+		mhdp->plugged = true;
+		spin_unlock(&mhdp->start_lock);
+		wake_up(&mhdp->fw_load_wq);
 		return;
 	}

